    "output": "Reviewer test: blocked, with evidence 'Factory citation unavailable: no factory record eligible for the cited stage, SHA, identity and command.' (expect toBe(\"met\") fails). Control test, same run record, evidence 'Attempted bun test: EPERM in sandbox': met, citing 'Factory covering test x.test.ts \u203a Factory gate literal title passed at aaaa\u2026 (stage 13)'. 1 pass, 1 fail."
   },
   "evidence": "At head, src/pipeline/gate-evidence.ts:162 has `const factoryClaim = /Factory (?:gate(?! substitution unavailable:)|covering test)\\b/gi;`. At ~233 `if (blocked.gateEvidence || blocked.evidence.search(factoryClaim) >= 0)` sends any row whose free-text evidence contains the phrase (case-insensitive) to citationRefusal. That function's loop at ~195-207 requires every match to begin a complete citation issued by the factory, otherwise it returns 'no factory record eligible\u2026', and the row is forced back to blocked before the covering-test binding runs. The base commit has no covering-test binding, so this false refusal is new in the change."
